+		// during the recording, the DMA wrote about 44100 words into it, and the stored sample holds
+		// 44100 samples drawn from only 7222 DISTINCT ramp values. The first two agree; the third says
+		// the output repeats each input roughly six times. All three cannot be true of one path.
+		//
+		// And the obvious explanation is already ruled out by measurement: pop() returns false when
+		// starved and the ramp does not advance on that path, so a starving FIFO would fake exactly
+		// this - but ADC-HEALTH reports starved=0 for the entire session. The ramp advances once per
+		// DMA word, as designed.
+		//
